<title>BELGIUM: Colruyt H1 profit rises to 1.1 bln bfr.</title>
<headline>Colruyt H1 profit rises to 1.1 bln bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996/1997 earnings</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			  1.105 vs     0.990</p>
<p>    Turnover (excluding VAT)	    33.007 vs    28.543</p>
<p>NOTE - Colruyt NV is Belgium's third largest retailer.  </p>
<p>    Cons cashflow			    2.310 vs     2.068</p>
<p>    Cons pre-tax profit		    1.605 vs     1.359</p>
<p>Note - Colruyt's financial year runs to March 31.</p>
<p>Colruyt said in a statement that consolidated turnover which was comparable with the previous year - by excluding Ripotot France - was 31.1 billion Belgian francs.</p>
<p>It said the turnover and results from the sectors Dolmen Computer Applications, Druco and Droomland were developing favourably and were in line with forecasts.</p>
<p>For the first nine months of the 1996/1997 financial year, turnover at Colruyt sales outlets increased eight percent, in line with forecasts, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
